sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant A as User A
    participant B as User B
    participant S as Saga + SeatService
    participant DB as MySQL (seats row)

    par simultaneous requests for seat 7
        A->>S: POST /api/bookings (key-A, seat 7)
        B->>S: POST /api/bookings (key-B, seat 7)
    end
    S->>DB: A: UPDATE seats SET TEMPORARILY_LOCKED ... WHERE id=7 AND status='AVAILABLE'
    S->>DB: B: UPDATE seats SET TEMPORARILY_LOCKED ... WHERE id=7 AND status='AVAILABLE'
    Note over DB: InnoDB row lock: the updates run one after the other
    DB-->>S: A: 1 row affected (WINNER)
    DB-->>S: B: 0 rows affected (status no longer AVAILABLE)
    S-->>B: 409 SEAT_UNAVAILABLE (booking cancelled, never charged)
    S->>S: A: charge payment (simulated)
    S->>DB: A: UPDATE seats SET BOOKED WHERE locked_by=A AND status='TEMPORARILY_LOCKED' AND locked_until > now
    DB-->>S: 1 row affected
    S-->>A: 201 booking CONFIRMED
